desc:NES Master Mixer - Hardware-accurate DAC (stereo: L=Pulse sum, R=TND weighted sum)
tags:mixer chiptune NES hardware-accurate DAC

in_pin:Pulse sum (L)
in_pin:TND weighted sum (R)
out_pin:Master L
out_pin:Master R

// ===================================================================
// Goes on a bus track that receives from all per-channel NES tracks:
//
//   Pulse 1  -> pan -1 -> bus L input
//   Pulse 2  -> pan -1 -> bus L input
//   Triangle -> pan +1 -> bus R input (with AUXRECV vol 0.00365)
//   Noise    -> pan +1 -> bus R input (with AUXRECV vol 0.00245)
//   DMC      -> pan +1 -> bus R input (with AUXRECV vol 0.01122)
//
// The per-channel tracks pan their output so pulses land on bus L and
// triangle/noise/DMC land on bus R. Per-track AUXRECV volume is chosen
// so the TND channels arrive already WEIGHTED (tri/8227, noise/12241,
// dmc/22638) -- this matches the NES hardware TND DAC formula.
//
// At this JSFX:
//   spl0 (L) = pulse1 + pulse2 summed linearly (range 0..1 where 1 = both at max vol)
//   spl1 (R) = tri/8227 + noise/12241 + dmc/22638 summed linearly
//
// Hardware DAC math:
//   Pulse pin: out = 95.88 * S / (8128 + 100 * S), S = sq1+sq2 (0..30)
//     In audio units where L = S/30:
//       out = 2876.4 * |L| / (8128 + 3000 * |L|)
//   TND pin:   out = 159.79 * W / (1 + 100 * W), W = tri/8227 + noise/12241 + dmc/22638
//     In audio units R represents W directly (thanks to per-track weighting):
//       out = 159.79 * |R| / (1 + 100 * |R|)
//
// Master output = pulse_dac + tnd_dac (linear sum, matches real NES two-pin topology).
//
// Per-channel tracks remain fully editable: mute/solo/FX/automation work normally.
// Pulses panned hard left and TND hard right is cosmetic routing only; the bus
// recombines them to mono master output.
// ===================================================================

slider1:1.5<0,4,0.01>Master Gain
slider2:1<0,2,0.01>Pulse Gain (DAC output scale)
slider3:1<0,2,0.01>TND Gain (DAC output scale)
slider4:1<0,1,1{Off,On}>Bypass (passthrough)
slider5:1<0,1,1{Off,On}>Remove DC Offset

@init
// DC blocker (1-pole HP ~10 Hz) for each audio input.
// NES per-channel plugin outputs have small DC offsets; strip before mixing.
hp_coef = exp(-2 * $pi * 10 / srate);
l_x = 0; l_y = 0;
r_x = 0; r_y = 0;

// Pulse DAC transfer: S = 30 * |L|, formula collapsed to single expression
function pulse_dac(L)
  local(aL, denom) (
  aL = abs(L);
  denom = 8128 + 3000 * aL;
  denom < 0.001 ? 0 : (L < 0 ? -1 : 1) * 2876.4 * aL / denom;
);

// TND DAC transfer: W = |R|
function tnd_dac(R)
  local(aR, denom) (
  aR = abs(R);
  denom = 1 + 100 * aR;
  denom < 0.001 ? 0 : (R < 0 ? -1 : 1) * 159.79 * aR / denom;
);

@slider
master_gain = slider1;
pulse_g = slider2;
tnd_g = slider3;
bypass_on = slider4;
dc_remove = slider5;

@sample
bypass_on ? (
  // Passthrough: sum L+R to mono, pass to both channels
  m = (spl0 + spl1) * master_gain;
  spl0 = m; spl1 = m;
) : (
  // DC block both inputs (removes unipolar DAC offset from per-channel plugins)
  dc_remove ? (
    l_y = hp_coef * (l_y + spl0 - l_x); l_x = spl0;
    r_y = hp_coef * (r_y + spl1 - r_x); r_x = spl1;
    l_in = l_y;
    r_in = r_y;
  ) : (
    l_in = spl0;
    r_in = spl1;
  );

  // Apply per-pin nonlinear DAC to pulse sum (L) and TND weighted sum (R)
  pulse_out = pulse_dac(l_in) * pulse_g;
  tnd_out = tnd_dac(r_in) * tnd_g;

  // Mix the two DAC pins (linear sum, matches hardware)
  mono_out = (pulse_out + tnd_out) * master_gain;
  spl0 = mono_out;
  spl1 = mono_out;
);
